ents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-16T10:11:35Z","updated_at":"2013-12-16T10:17:00Z","body":"You are correct on the first half of that statement. I'm actually looking at it right now and noticed that. The `--stream` option has nothing to do with this. Previous to the commit in Pull Request #187, the content is always streamed from the server. I changed it so that it would always download all of the content. A timeout will not be honored if streaming occurs. I've tested this with [httpbin.org/delay/n](http://httpbin.org). Try the following command.\n\n```\n$ python3 -c \"import requests; response = requests.get('http://httpbin.org/delay/3', stream=True, timeout=1); print(response)\"\n```\n\nThen try it without streaming.\n\n```\n$ python3 -c \"import requests; response = requests.get('http://httpbin.org/delay/3', timeout=1); print(response)\"\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/httpie/cli/issues/comments/30649041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"tylercrompton","id":997507,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NzUwNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/997507?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton","html_url":"https://github.com/tylercrompton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylercrompton/orgs","rep